# Kettlebell Workout App Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Build an offline-capable web app, installed on an iPhone Home Screen, that generates a kettlebell workout from the available bells, chosen movement patterns and available minutes, then walks through it one exercise at a time.

**Architecture:** All logic runs on the device. A pure, seeded rules engine turns a request plus the exercise database into a flat list of steps; the UI walks that list and holds no programming logic. Kit profiles, history and the in-progress workout live in `localStorage`. No server, no database, no API keys.

**Tech Stack:** Next.js 15 (App Router), TypeScript strict, Tailwind CSS v4, Vitest, Serwist for the service worker, `sharp` for the one-off image slicing script. No animation library: CSS transitions cover everything here.

## Global Constraints

- Source spec is `docs/SPEC.md`. Where this plan and the spec disagree, the spec wins and the plan is corrected.
- TypeScript `strict: true`. No `any` in `src/lib`.
- Everything under `src/lib/` is pure: no `Date.now()`, no `Math.random()`, no `window`, no `fetch`. Clock and storage access live in `src/lib/storage.ts` and in components only.
- Randomness comes only from the seeded generator in `src/lib/rng.ts`.
- Movement patterns are exactly: `hinge`, `squat`, `push`, `pull`, `carry`, `core`.
- Levels are exactly: `beginner`, `intermediate`, `advanced`.
- Exercise `id` is kebab-case, is stable, and matches its image filename: `public/exercises/<id>.webp`.
- `localStorage` keys are exactly `kb.kits.v1`, `kb.history.v1`, `kb.prefs.v1`, `kb.active.v1`.
- Colours, spacing and type come from the CSS custom properties defined in Task 10. No raw hex values in components.
- Tap targets at least 44px. Text contrast at WCAG AA. Honour `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- British English in all user-facing copy.
- Commit after every task. Conventional Commits style.

## File structure

```
PROJECTS/kettlebell-app/
  docs/SPEC.md, PLAN.md, image-brief.md
  media-source/grid-01.png            # the supplied 4x4 sheet
  scripts/slice-grid.mjs              # one-off, cuts the sheet into 16 stills
  scripts/check-media.mjs             # lists exercises with no image
  public/exercises/<id>.webp
  public/manifest.webmanifest, icons
  src/lib/
    types.ts        # every shared type, no logic
    rng.ts          # seeded random, pick, shuffle
    kit.ts          # kit profiles, load band -> real bell
    pool.ts         # filter exercises and combos by request and kit
    budget.ts       # split the minutes into three blocks
    format.ts       # circuit | complex | strength
    select.ts       # choose the exercises for the main block
    prescribe.ts    # reps, rest, duration estimate
    fit.ts          # search rounds and counts to hit the time budget
    flatten.ts      # blocks -> ordered Step[]
    generate.ts     # the one public entry point
    storage.ts      # localStorage, the only impure module in lib
    data/exercises.ts, data/combos.ts, data/warmups.ts
  src/components/   # Button, Card, Chip, Ring, ProgressBar, ExerciseCard, RestCard
  src/app/          # App Router pages, one per screen
  tests/            # mirrors src/lib
```

Files split by responsibility, not by layer. Each `src/lib` module is small enough to hold in context and is tested on its own.

